  "details": "I created little explanation how networking in VRChat should be working. The first image is how it is working now and the second is how it should works. Actually VRChat is using one server in America, that means low latency between users in America but high latency between Eurpean users and between American and Eurpean users.\nSolution on the second image uses two or more servers for reducing latency between users in region. It can also reduce bandwith because you can marge data transfer in one regional server and send it to the second one where data will be saperated for each user in region.\n\nI know, make it happen will be difficult but it can really improve experience for non American users. I have also another idea for better cpu performance that can be possible with bandwidth improvement of this networking model. This improvement is like in previous update where you tried compute IK on one client and send it to others. But it can be better if you send whole avatar skeleton after IK and Dynamic Bones computation are done. That means if user have avatar with lots of DynBones it will lagging only for him.",
